# SRG-APP-000092-WSR-000055  -  CAT II
# The web server must initiate session logging upon start up.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000092-WSR-000055
group:           V-206357
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-001464
control_rev5:    AU-14

contribution:    Splunk Web opens its HTTP access log when the application server starts,
                 and splunkd records REST access in splunkd_access.log from the same
                 moment; the application configures which log receives that traffic and
                 that no endpoint is excluded from it.

governs:         restmap.conf - The management interface endpoints, and which clients may reach them.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           restmap.conf [] includeInAccessLog not_equals false
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] log.access_file https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] log.access_file non_empty
                 reason: "log.access_file = <filename>. The HTTP access log filename. This
                         file is written in the default $SPLUNK_HOME/var/log directory.
                         Default: web_access.log" Related shipped settings:
                         log.access_maxsize = 25000000 and log.access_maxfiles = 5.
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The operating system's service manager decides when splunkd and Splunk Web
                 start, so whether logging begins at system boot depends on the boot-start
                 configuration, not on the application.

citation:        INVENTION. Removed web.conf [settings] appServerPorts not_equals 0.
                 web.conf.spec defines the setting as "appServerPorts = <positive
                 integer>[, <positive integer>...]" and states "At one time, setting this
                 to zero indicated that the web service should be run in a legacy mode as a
                 separate service, but as of Splunk 8.0 this is no longer supported." Zero
                 is outside the permitted vocabulary on 10.4.2, so the condition tests a
                 state the product cannot be in and contributes no evidence; neither the
                 check nor the fix text mentions it. The restmap placeholder stanza was
                 replaced with the empty stanza the determined row carries.
finding:         The web tier's access logging is not fully configured - no access log is
                 named, or a REST endpoint is excluded from splunkd_access.log - so logging
                 does not capture all requests from the moment the application server
                 starts.
